/* ============================================================
   ICONS — HugeIcons (MIT), the STROKE ROUNDED style: open 1.5px
   strokes with rounded caps and joins on a `0 0 24 24` box.
   Google's Material *Symbols* cut this file used to run on was
   replaced platform-wide on 15 Sep 2026 (Maryam), after
   confirming HugeIcons' free Stroke-Rounded set (MIT,
   `@hugeicons/core-free-icons@4.3.3`, 6,025 free glyphs) covers
   every UI mark the four portals draw. Every glyph below is
   pasted from that package rather than drawn, so the platform is
   one optical family and nothing is kept in sync by hand.

   TWO THINGS CHANGED AT ONCE, and either alone breaks a call
   site silently.

   1. THE GRID. HugeIcons are `0 0 24 24`; the Material Symbols
      before them were `0 -960 960 960`. A path in the wrong box
      renders as an invisible speck with nothing thrown (trap 7).
      The `0 0 24 24` box is now the NORM — `grep viewBox` should
      find it almost everywhere; the `0 -960 960 960` box is now
      the EXCEPTION, kept only by the filled marks below (and by
      Maryam's own `talChat`, which was regridded to 960 to join
      the family it was drawn for and stays there).

   2. THE PAINT. Material glyphs were FILLED paths coloured by CSS
      `fill:`. HugeIcons are OPEN STROKES: they need `stroke:` and
      `fill:none`. So the icon colour system moved off `fill:` to
      `color:` / `currentColor` — each glyph below is stored as
      self-painted inner markup (`stroke="currentColor"
      fill="none"`, or `fill="currentColor"` for the retained
      filled marks), and the ~300 CSS icon rules across the layers
      now say `color:` instead of `fill:`. Chart / ring / effect
      fills are NOT icons and keep `fill`/`stroke` untouched.

   THE FILLED MARKS STAY ON MATERIAL — DELIBERATELY, FOR NOW.
   HugeIcons' free tier is stroke-only; its solid/filled style is
   Pro. FILL is a STATE axis (a lit rating slot, a done tick, a
   solid stop), and a HugeIcons outline shown beside a Material
   solid in the SAME widget would read as broken. So each filled
   state-mark AND its outline partner stay on the 960 grid / fill
   model until the filled set is sourced separately:

     star / starOutline        a rating's lit and unlit slots
     checkFilled / checkOutline done vs not-done
     stopFilled                 a solid dot
     thumbsUp / thumbsUpFilled  a vote toggle
     thumbsDown / thumbsDownFilled

   These ten keys are listed in BOX960 below; the proxy paints
   them on the 960 box with `fill="currentColor"`. Everything
   else is a HugeIcons stroke glyph on the 24 box.

   STILL NOT HERE, all deliberately: the Phosphor duotone `P` set
   (the Points list, a different family on a 256 box — see its own
   note below), and the brand marks `CHEV` / `TN_MARK` /
   `TN_CHEVRONS` / `ARROW_LINE`, which carry their own boxes.
   ============================================================ */
